<p>Iran’s Revolutionary Guards said they would target major U.S. technology companies if more Iranian leaders were killed, naming firms including Apple, Google, and Meta and warning that attacks could begin from 8 p.m. Tehran time on April 1. Several outlets said government-backed Iranian media carried the statement, which framed the threat as retaliation for what Iran called “targeted assassinations” and alleged that 18 companies were complicit in tracking Iranian officials. The warning comes amid a wider U.S.-Israel-Iran conflict in which NDTV reported that more than 3,000 people had been killed. The White House responded that the U.S. military was prepared to thwart any Iranian attacks, and one official said recent U.S. actions had contributed to a sharp drop in Iranian ballistic missile and drone attacks. The episode adds a new corporate and regional security dimension to an already dangerous confrontation in the Middle East.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/bltkBJw2R8v-UXE4bFYclcZv6NQEqZd82rNJC3_vFKrwVvEVW2S_8c9W3lWAVAVkXq7QO-WvKXYRejyeDclOcTndAlGf8SbWjzOrRROHDgwaTzZTCNJZzUOMMLw-K6n22O2dns2CLy08JLC6FCDHGguLkTHJUpJ8dwvIyMW8bgnZZCGOXpvDrR-e' alt='Image accompanying coverage of Iran’s warning that it may target U.S. tech firms if more leaders are killed' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Defense scope: Politico reported that the warning also covered American defense companies, widening the threat beyond consumer technology firms.</li><li>Worker warning: The IRGC urged employees of the named institutions to leave their workplaces immediately to preserve their lives, underscoring the immediacy of the threat.</li><li>Regional location: Politico reported that the threatened companies were described as operating in the Middle East, focusing attention on regional offices and infrastructure rather than only U.S. headquarters.</li><li>Retaliation formula: SCMP reported that the Guards said the companies should expect destruction of their “relevant units” for every future assassination in Iran, framing the threat as a one-for-one response.</li></ul><blockquote>The United States military is and was prepared to curtail any attacks by Iran, as evidenced by the 90 percent drop in ballistic missile and drone attacks by the terrorist regime - White House official</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps: The IRGC cast the warning as a deterrent, arguing that U.S.-linked companies would be held accountable if assassinations of Iranian leaders continued. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3348585/iran-says-will-target-apple-google-and-meta-if-more-its-leaders-killed'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>White House: Washington answered the corporate threat with a force-protection message rather than directly rebutting Iran’s allegations against the companies, emphasizing U.S. military readiness and reduced Iranian strike activity. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/iran-war-news-us-forces-ready-white-house-replies-to-irans-strike-warning-to-tech-firms-11294166#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>, <a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/us-ready-thwart-iran-attacks-after-irgc-threats-american-firms'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>Iranian state-backed media account: By distributing the warning through Tasnim, Iranian authorities signaled that they were presenting the threat as an officially backed message to U.S.-linked businesses in the region, not as an isolated comment. (<a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/03/31/iran-threatens-to-target-us-owned-infrastructure-in-the-middle-east-00852120'>Politico</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/worldnews/comments/1s8xmc4/iran_threatens_to_attack_us_tech_companies/'>Iran Threatens to Attack U.S. Tech Companies Starting April 1</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/iran-guards-say-will-target-us-tech-firms-if-more-leaders-killed/article70808810.ece'>Iran Guards say will target U.S. tech firms if more leaders killed</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3348585/iran-says-will-target-apple-google-and-meta-if-more-its-leaders-are-killed'>Iran says will target Apple, Google and Meta if more of its leaders are killed</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/us-israel-iran-war-live-updates-pakistan-to-hold-regional-meeting-on-ending-iran-war-middle-east-conflict-saudi-arabia-turkey-egypt-strait-of-hormuz-11281097#publisher=newsstand'>US Israel Iran War LIVE: Iran Guards Say Will Target US Tech Firms If More Leaders Killed</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/iran-guards-threaten-to-target-us-tech-firms-if-more-leaders-killed'>Iran threatens to target US tech firms if more of its leaders are killed</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/03/31/iran-threatens-to-target-us-owned-infrastructure-in-the-middle-east-00852120'>Iran threatens to strike US-owned tech companies in the Middle East</a> - politico.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/us-ready-thwart-iran-attacks-after-irgc-threats-american-firms'>US ready to thwart Iran attacks after IRGC threats to American firms</a> - al-monitor.com</li></ul>